# backend/.dockerignore — T-03.1 (SPEC-004 s3.6, ADR-032/D2)
#
# The five entries the plan names, literally: `.venv`, `tests/`, `data/`, `.env*`,
# `__pycache__`. `.env*` is the one D3.6/D3.8 morde on — without it, a secret placed at
# `backend/.env` during a local build would be COPYable into the image.
.venv
tests/
data/
.env*
__pycache__

# Housekeeping — build artifacts and VCS metadata that add nothing to a Python image and
# were never named in the Dockerfile's COPY list anyway, but keeping them out of the build
# context also keeps it small and avoids ever tempting a future broad `COPY . .`.
.git
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
